    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0054" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v07p1/pg18"/>

                <head>10. Telegram From the Embassy in Finland to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d10-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Helsinki</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-03-06T16:00:00+02:00">March 6, 1958, 4
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>537. Prime Minister<anchor n="1" xml:id="d10-f2"/> informs me in substance as
                    follows: “If OEEC finds Finland satisfactory
                    for membership, we will join. It will take a little time to work out details.
                    Some Finnish officials are hesitant because of local Communist press criticism,
                    but we have had no adverse comments from Soviet Government or Soviet press, and
                    they must have known about this for months. In any event I intend to continue to
                    press for early and favorable action.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Hickerson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d10-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d10-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 840.00/3–658. Confidential. Repeated
                    to Moscow and Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d10-f2" n="1" xml:id="d10-f2-content">
                <p>Urho Kekkonen.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
